  "title": "Iran and U.S. Reopen Hormuz Strait Amid Diplomatic Struggles",
  "summary": "Iran and the U.S. are poised to end the war with a new peace deal, but the countries appear far apart, with talks focusing on reopening the Strait of Hormuz and lifting a US blockade on Iran, while the deadline is expiring. The conflict has stalled for over five months, with both sides pushing for different approaches to resolve the crisis.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "Iran's president denies threatening to resign during talks over the Strait of Hormuz, while the U.S. and Qatar report progress on a ceasefire and the reopening of the strait, though shipping remains blocked.",
